     H*  04/15/94 C:20  REQ/PROJ: 128/FS127                          **
     H*                 1. SCR01 - ADD BILL SUB-TYPE TO SCREEN.      **
     H*                    ONLY ALLOWED WITH 'H' BILL TYPE ALL OTHERS**
     H*                    WILL PRODUCE AN ERROR.                    **
     H*                 2. F9(SCR03) USE VALUE IN H1RECF FOR THE     **
     H*                    SCREEN WE SHOULD RETURN TO.  H1RECF IS    **
     H*                    LOADED IN SCR01T WHEN WE DECIDE WHICH     **
     H*                    SCREEN WE ARE GOING TO.                   **
     H*                 3. IF PROVIDER TYPE IS A '4', THE USER WILL  **
     H*                    BE ABLE TO ENTER A BILL SUB-TYPE CODE.    **
     H*                    ENTRY OF THIS CODE WILL ALLOW CERTAIN     **
     H*                    CONDITIONS TO ADVANCE A HOSPITAL PROVIDER **
     H*                    TO SCR02 FOR ENTRY OF DETAIL CHARGES.     **
     H*                    ONCE WE KNOW THE AJUDICATION STATE WE WILL**
     H*                    VERIFY THE ENTERED BILL SUB-TYPE AGAINST  **
     H*                    VALUES FOR THAT STATE(STSTP).  IF THE     **
     H*                    BILL SUB-TYPE EXISTS, WE WILL USE THE     **
     H*                    CORRESPONDING SCREEN VALUE ENTERED FOR    **
     H*                    THAT BILL SUB-TYPE CODE.                  **
     H*                 4. SCR01 - ADD PROVIDER ALPHA SEARCH(F19)    **
     H*                 5. SCR02/SCR04/SCRRX - ADD DIAGNOSIS CODE    **
     H*                    ALPHA SEARCH(F16)                         **
     H*                 6. SCR03 - ADDED OPTION 8=PRE-CERT INQUIRY   **
     H*                    THIS IS CONDITIONED ON PRE-CERT BEING     **
     H*                    INSTALLED(*IN11=1).  A PRE-CERT MUST BE   **
     H*                    SELECTED ON SCR02/SCR04/SCRRX BEFORE THIS **
     H*                    OPTION IS AVAILABLE.                      **
     H*                 7. WRIT 2,4,X - UPDATE CARCFL FLAG IN THE    **
     H*                    FOLLOWING WAYS:                           **
     H*                    A) Y = REASONABLE AND CUSTOMARY CODE      **
     H*                    B) S = SERVICE CODE                       **
     H*                    C) C = CPT4 PROCEDURE CODE                **
     H*                    D) X = PHARMACY CODE                      **
     H*                    E) N = NO MATCH FMSVPxx USE FDHCP FILE    **
     H*                 8. THROUGHOUT PROGRAM - WHEN DECIDING WHICH  **
     H*                    FILE TO USE(FMPRPxx, FMSVPxx, FMRCP) WE   **
     H*                    WILL USE xxRCFL TO DECIDE WHERE TO GET    **
     H*                    DESCRIPTION AND OTHER INFORMATION FROM:   **
     H*                    RCFL       FILE TO USE     CAUSE          **
     H*                     X         FDHCP           PHARMACY CODE  **
     H*                     Y         FMRCP           R&C CODE       **
     H*                     C         FMPRPxx         PROCEDURE CODE **
     H*                     S         FMSVPxx         SERVICE CODE   **
     H*                     N         FDHCP           NOT IN FMSVP   **
     H*                 9. WHEN UNPENDING CHARGES AND GOING TO SCR03 **
     H*                    WE WILL LOAD THE CORRECT VALUE INTO H1RECF**
     H*                    DEPENDING ON THE TYPE OF CHARGES WE JUST  **
     H*                    UNPENDED AND ADJUDICATED.  BASED ON THE   **
     H*                    FOLLOWING:                                **
     H*                    DCPRTY     DCBLTY          SCREEN VALUE   **
     H*                       P         P                SCR02       **
     H*                       H         H                SCR04       **
     H*                       H         P                SCR02       **
     H*                       P         X                SCRRX       **
     H*                10. IF WE ARE GOING TO SCR04 WE MUST LOOK AT  **
     H*                    STATE FILE(STSTP) TO SEE IF THIS STATE WE **
     H*                    ARE PROCESSING AGAINST WILL ALLOW CPT4    **
     H*                    CODES ON SCR04(ST1A2=Y).  IF THIS FLAG IS **
     H*                    A 'Y' WE WILL DISPLAY/ALLOW CPT4 CODES AND**
     H*                    SEARCHES F5=R&C CODE SEARCH AND F6=PROC   **
     H*                    CODE SEARCH.                              **
     H*                11. TO DECIDE WHAT VALUE TO WRITE TO CARCFL   **
     H*                    FROM SCR04(FOR STATES THAT CAN ENTER CPT4)**
     H*                    WE WILL:                                  **
     H*                    A) IF HIT IN FMSVPxx LOAD CARCFL = S      **
     H*                    B) IF HIT IN FMPRPxx LOAD CARCFL = C      **
     H*                    C) IF HIT IN FMRCP LOAD CARCFL = Y        **
     H*                    D) IF NOT HIT IN FMSVPxx, FMPRPxx, FMRCP  **
     H*                       CARCFL = N                             **
     H*                12. THERE WILL NOT BE THE USE OF PROCEDURE    **
     H*                    CODE MODIFIER FROM SCR04 FOR CPT4 CODES   **
     H*                    ENDTERED.                                 **
     H*                13. UNIT WILL WORK THE SAME WAY FOR CPT4 CODES**
     H*                    ON SCR04 AS IT DOES FOR SERVICE CODES.  IT**
     H*                    WILL GO BY THE CHART LISTED AT TOP OF PGM.**
     H*                14. DCSR - IF CHARGES ARE UNPENDED WE WILL    **
     H*                    UPDATE DC10A1(1ST 5 POSITIONS) WITH THE   **
     H*                    CURRENT NETWORK CODE(SCNWCD).  WE DO NOT  **
     H*                    WANT TO PROCESS CHARGES AGAINST CURRENT   **
     H*                    NETWORK CODE AND HAVE OLD NETWORK CODE    **
     H*                    LOADED IN FADCP RECORD.                   **
     H*                15. SCR05T - ALLOW ENTRY OF NEGATIVE REDUCTION**
     H*                    AMOUNT.  CHANGED EDIT CODE TO 'M' SO THE  **
     H*                    NEGATIVE SIGN WILL APPEAR.  IF TOTP IS    **
     H*                    GREATER THAN TOTC AND ALL REDUCTIONS      **
     H*                    FIELDS ARE EQUAL TO ZEROS THE DIFFERENCE  **
     H*                    WILL BE DUMPED INTO MRA REDUCTONS AS A    **
     H*                    NEGATIVE REDUCTIONS.                      **
